According to a report by IntelMarketResearch, the global Amine Oxide Market was valued at USD 242 million in 2024 and is projected to grow from USD 265 million in 2025 to USD 460 million by 2032, exhibiting a CAGR of 9.9% during the forecast period.
Amine oxides are chemical compounds used extensively as surfactants in personal care, household cleaning, and industrial formulations. Their foaming, thickening, and emulsifying properties make them useful ingredients in products such as shampoos, liquid soaps, detergents, and specialized chemical formulations.
